<title>UK: UK's Nat Express surprised at DTI decision.</title>
<headline>UK's Nat Express surprised at DTI decision.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's National Express Group said on Thursday it was surprised at the government's decision to refer the acquisitions of two rail franchises to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission but said it was happy to talk to the authorities.</p>
<p>The new Trade and Industry Secretary Margaret Beckett said earlier she was referring National's planned purchase of regional ScotRail network and the Central Trains Ltd franchise in the West Midlands to the MMC.</p>
<p>National Express' share price fell 28 1/2 pence to 490 1/2 after Beckett's announcement came in.</p>
